cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below and identify the version used."
title: "Hierarchical Statistical Analyzer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Terreau"
    given-names: "Sébastien"
version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
# Zenodo concept DOI: represents all versions of this software.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19500564
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienleonmichel/hierarchical-statistical-analyzer"
url: "https://github.com/sebastienleonmichel/hierarchical-statistical-analyzer/releases/tag/v4.0.0"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  GUI-based Python framework for hierarchical and replicate-aware
  statistical analysis of biological datasets using global and pairwise
  stratified rank permutation tests, block-aware effect summaries, and
  linear mixed-effects models with fixed condition and categorical
  experiment effects and a random intercept for each experiment by
  condition sample.
keywords:
  - "hierarchical statistics"
  - "linear mixed model"
  - "stratified Wilcoxon"
  - "van Elteren"
  - "permutation test"
  - "biostatistics"
  - "replicate-aware analysis"
  - "mixed-effects modeling"
  - "nested observations"
  - "experiment blocking"
